  "id": "convergent-production",
  "term": "convergent production",
  "definition": "Convergent production is the independent development of very similar, specialized ways of making things in different groups or places. In this source, it refers to stone-tool manufacturing methods that closely resemble one another even though they arose under different circumstances and may have served different purposes or meanings.",
